# Build output: `npm run build` in web/ writes straight into worker/public, and
# `wrangler deploy` uploads it from there. It is generated, so it is not source.
#
# Consequence for CI: a Cloudflare Workers Build must build the frontend itself,
# or it will deploy a Worker with an empty assets directory and the dashboard
# will 404. Settings that work from the repo root:
#     build:  npm --prefix web ci && npm --prefix web run build
#     deploy: npx wrangler deploy -c worker/wrangler.toml
worker/public/

# Local data: fetched bytes and generated SQL are reproducible, not source
ingest/cache/
ingest/out/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# The SQLite store lives on the orphan branch `pipeline-state`, not in main's
# history - see docs/RUNBOOK.md. A local refresh writes here; keep it out.
#
# ANCHORED. Unanchored `data/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth,
# which silently swallowed web/public/data - the exported JSON the dashboard
# reads and the refresh commits. The leading slash is load-bearing.
# CONTENTS, not the directory. `/data/` excludes the directory itself, and git
# will not descend into an excluded directory - so a later `!` cannot re-include
# anything under it. That is why this is `/data/*` with a hole punched in it.
/data/*
!/data/raw/
/data/raw/*
!/data/raw/*.jsonl

# data/raw/*.jsonl IS THE STORE OF RECORD. It stopped being a local artefact
# when the dashboard left D1: the SQLite file is rebuilt from it on every run,
# and every monthly refresh arrives as a diff in it. Losing it loses
# raw_revenue_history and the original first_seen_utc timestamps, and neither
# can be re-scraped - MOPS serves today's version of a filing, not the version
# it served in March.
#
# data/pipeline.sqlite stays ignored: binary, rebuilt from the JSONL, and it
# would churn the whole file on every write.

# Scratch CSV dumps from verifying the export against the API.
/exp.csv
